## Protocol

### 1. Infer intent from the opening command phrase

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Match this mission’s command phrases and prepare routing.
- **Inputs:** Opening message; **`mission.yaml`** `commands`.
- **Expected output:** Intent label (`author-multi-part`).
- **Next-step resolution:** Phrase matches → §2 (auto-advance). No match →
  USER_CHECKPOINT below.

USER_CHECKPOINT — confirm intent when the opening command phrase does not match unambiguously.

- Apply **phrase matching** from [`.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/4_mission.mdc`](.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/4_mission.mdc)
  (longer phrases first).
- Map phrases from **`mission.yaml`**:
  - **`author multi-part document`** → intent **`author-multi-part`**
- After intent is mapped, run **Dispatch display refresh** when scope is readable.

### 2. Resolve documentation folder and target file context

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Bind this dispatch to a registered documentation folder and the
  multi-part document path (new or existing).
- **Inputs:** [`.sedea/documentation-management.yaml`](.sedea/documentation-management.yaml);
  intent from §1; user hints (folder slug, relative file path).
- **Expected output:** `folderSlug`, `localPath`, `rclone.remote`,
  `rclone.remotePath`; `relativeFilePath` under `localPath` when known.
  When §3 used a template, `relativeFilePath` **must** be the duplicated
  working file — **never** the template path.
- **Next-step resolution:** Folder resolved → §3. Missing registry or tools →
  USER_CHECKPOINT below.

Read the folder registry completely. Do **not** invent slugs, remotes, or local
roots. Preconditions follow
[`.sedea/centers/documentation-management/rules/00_documentation-management.mdc`](../../rules/00_documentation-management.mdc)
and
[`.sedea/centers/documentation-management/rules/10_required-tools.mdc`](../../rules/10_required-tools.mdc).

USER_CHECKPOINT — pick registered folder slug · provide relative file path · start Required Tools Installation in a new dispatch · abort.

### 3. Intake — template or structure

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Collect how the multi-part document is shaped before master planning.
- **Inputs:** Folder binding from §2; optional template path; optional structure
  outline from the user.
- **Expected output:** `intakeMode` = `template` | `structure-given`; when
  `template`: `templatePath` (read-only source) + `relativeFilePath` (new working
  document under `localPath`); when `structure-given`: approved structure outline;
  optional existing document to extend (non-template path only).
- **Next-step resolution:** Intake approved with a writable working document → §4.
  Incomplete → re-ask.

USER_CHECKPOINT — use template · supply structure outline · revise intake · abort.

**Modes (binding):**

| Mode | Outcome |
|------|---------|
| **Use template** | User supplies `templatePath`. Agent **duplicates** the template into a **new** working document under `localPath` (propose a new filename; confirm or revise before write). Master plan and all later edits target **only** the new file. |
| **Structure given** | User supplies section/part structure; master plan uses that outline on a new or existing **non-template** working file. |

**Template reuse (binding — Use template):**

1. Templates stay blank / reusable — **forbidden** to offer editing the template file, or to write part content / master-plan body into `templatePath`.
2. Before collecting document content or spawning part lanes, **propose a new filename** (and optional subfolder under `localPath`) via structured choice; after confirmation, **copy** the template to that path and set `relativeFilePath` to the copy.
3. Treat `templatePath` as **read-only** for structure derivation only (section headings / outline). All authoring, Generate Content, Sync of the working doc, and PDF export use `relativeFilePath`.
4. Mirror Author Simple Document create mode **Use template** → scaffold a **standard document** from the template (non-template outcome).

**Forbidden:** editing the selected template in place; treating the template path as the multi-part working document; skipping the new-filename proposal when `intakeMode` is `template`.

### 4. Author and approve master plan (spawned master-plan lane)

- **Type:** Agent engagement and handover
- **execution:** `spawned` (leader → master-plan)
- **Intent:** After §3 intake, Squad Leader spawns **master-plan**; the child
  produces a reviewable **master plan**: document overview, ordered
  parts/sections, and high-level content notes — not full part prose.
- **Inputs:** Intake from §3 (`intakeMode`, `relativeFilePath`, optional
  `templatePath` / structure outline); folder binding (`localPath`, `folderSlug`,
  rclone fields); `operationsDocsDirectory`.
- **Expected output:** Child terminal with `masterPlanPath`; `parts[]` with
  stable `partId` / titles; `userApprovedMasterPlan: true`;
  `continuationStatus: terminal`.
- **Next-step resolution:** Child terminal → §5 standing options / §6 part loop.
  Rejected or aborted on child lane → USER_CHECKPOINT on leader (retry · abort).

**Procedure (binding)**

1. Squad Leader emits **`mission_control_spawn_agent`** for
   **`skills/master-plan/SKILL.md`** with §3 + folder binding inputs.
   Set spawn **`name`** to **`Master plan`** (or a ≤64-char document title when
   known); **`description`**: one-line scope (≤512 chars).
2. Open **#external-wait** on the leader before ending the turn (wait for
   master-plan terminal).
3. **On the master-plan lane** (see `skills/master-plan/SKILL.md`): draft artifact
   under dispatch **`plans/`**; resolve open questions via structured choice;
   **USER_CHECKPOINT** — approve master plan · revise master plan · abort.
4. On approval: register **`masterPlanPath`** via
   **`mission_control_update_relevant_documents`**; emit terminal
   **`mission_control_send_agent_result`**.
5. Squad Leader records `masterPlanPath` and `parts[]`, then routes to §5.

**Forbidden:** leader inline master-plan authoring; one-pass full-document
authoring on this step (that is Author Simple Document); Squad Leader
USER_CHECKPOINT to re-approve a plan already approved on the master-plan lane.

### 5. Standing options (Squad Leader — always while active)

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Keep long-running control options available between part deliveries.
- **Inputs:** Master plan; part completion ledger; sync/PDF state.
- **Expected output:** User-selected next action.
- **Next-step resolution:** Route per table below; re-open this gate after child
  terminals and after each part completes.

USER_CHECKPOINT — start/continue next part · request gap analysis · handle document review comments · Generate Content · Sync documents · Export PDF · approve all content / finish · pause.

| Option | Next |
|--------|------|
| **Start / continue next part** | §6 |
| **Request gap analysis** | §7 |
| **Handle document review comments** | §7a (leader opt-in gate) |
| **Generate Content** | §8 |
| **`sync-documents`** — Sync documents | §9 |
| **Export PDF** | §10 (Squad Leader only) |
| **Approve all content / finish** | §11 |
| **Pause** | Resumable wait; re-open §5 later |

### 5a. Always-on Sync on Squad Leader structured choice (binding)

After §2 folder bind succeeds, **every** Squad Leader
**`mission_control_present_structured_choice`** / **AskQuestion** modal on this
dispatch **must** include **Sync documents** until dispatch resolution.

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Option id** | `sync-documents` |
| **Label** | Sync documents |
| **Placement** | After mission-specific options; **before** the universal modal trailer (`more-details` … `other`) per rule **2** |

**Applies to:** §5 standing gate; §3 intake gate on the leader lane;
**#external-wait** resume modals while child lanes run; gap / content-generator /
PDF / sync failure gates on the **leader** lane — any Squad Leader gate after
folder bind.

**Forbidden:** omitting `sync-documents` from any Squad Leader modal after §2
folder bind; treating sync as available only on the §5 standing gate.

**On select `sync-documents`:** run §9. On success, **re-open the same gate**
that was active when sync started (same options and mission context). When sync
was selected from §5 as the primary next action, return to §5 after §9.

**Child lanes:** unchanged — Sync remains Squad Leader–owned (Squad operations
table).

### 5b. Relevant Links post-write registration (binding)

Mission Control **Relevant Links** do **not** auto-update from Write/StrReplace.
Every lane that creates or materially edits a file the developer should reopen
must call MCP **`mission_control_update_relevant_documents`** on the **calling
slot** in the **same turn** (or the next turn before StreamFinal).

Normative platform contract:
[`.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/9_display-metadata-authority.mdc`](.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/9_display-metadata-authority.mdc)
§ *Relevant Links / documents*. Mission skill detail:
[`skills/README.md`](skills/README.md) § *Relevant Links — post-write registration*.

| Call | Skip |
|------|------|
| Approved **master plan** (**master-plan** skill §4), **part plans**, **gap reports**, **review plans** under dispatch **`plans/`** or **`operationsDocsDirectory`** | Read-only `Read` / Grep |
| **SoT changes follow-up** docs and **conversation-review** evidence under **`operationsDocsDirectory`** | Paths already registered this session with no content change |
| **Working document** at **`localPath` + `relativeFilePath`** when materially edited | Warm-up manifests; transient scratch; build artifacts |

**Kind hints:** ops plans and reports → `plan` or `other`; working document →
`other` (optional **`label`** with part id or basename).

**Master-plan skill §4 (binding):** After the approved master plan is written on
the **master-plan** child lane, that lane registers its absolute path via
**`mission_control_update_relevant_documents`** — not the Squad Leader.

**Forbidden:** prose-only “add to Relevant Links”; registering every read path;
using display-metadata MCP (`mission_control_update_lane_display` /
`mission_control_update_dispatch_display`) for documents.

Per-skill post-write hooks live in each **`SKILL.md`** under
**`skills/`** — see the README table.

### 6. Part delivery loop (planner owns author)

- **Type:** Agent engagement and handover
- **execution:** `spawned` (nested: leader → part-planner → author)
- **Intent:** For the next incomplete part in the master plan, Squad Leader
  spawns **part-planner**; part-planner approves the part plan, then **spawns
  author** and owns plan-revision handoff to that author lane.
- **Inputs:** `partId` / part title from master plan; folder binding;
  `operationsDocsDirectory`; prior authored parts for context pointers.
- **Expected output:** Part plan approved; part content authored; optional SoT
  follow-up rows appended; ledger marks part complete or deferred.
- **Next-step resolution:** After part-planner terminal (which follows author
  terminal on the happy path) → §5. Failure → USER_CHECKPOINT.

**Procedure**

1. Squad Leader spawns **`skills/part-planner/SKILL.md`** with part identity and
   master-plan excerpt. Set spawn **`name`** to **`P{nn} — {partTitle}`** per
   **Part-planner lane title** above; **`description`**: one-line part scope
   (≤512 chars). Part plan shape is defined in that session (not fixed
   globally). **Forbidden on the happy path:** Squad Leader spawning **author**
   directly; spawn labels derived only from skill frontmatter **`name`**.
2. Open **#external-wait** resume options before ending the turn (wait for
   part-planner terminal).
3. **On the part-planner lane** (see `skills/part-planner/SKILL.md`): after the
   part plan is approved, emit **`mission_control_spawn_agent`** for
   **`skills/author/SKILL.md`** with `partPlanPath` and document binding. Keep
   **`continuationStatus: active`** until the author child finishes (or the part
   is deferred/aborted).
4. **Plan revisions (binding):** When the part plan changes after author spawn,
   **part-planner** pushes revision context to the **author** child — prefer
   **`mission_control_notify_child_lanes`** with `changeType: plan-revision` and
   `affectedPlanPaths` including `partPlanPath` when plan-change notification is
   enabled; otherwise same-lane re-handoff / updated `partPlanPath` without
   Squad Leader re-spawn. **Forbidden:** requiring Squad Leader to re-spawn
   author solely to deliver a plan revision.
5. On author terminal (`partComplete: true`, deferred, or failure), part-planner
   emits its own terminal result to Squad Leader (merged outputs include SoT
   follow-up fields from the author child). Leader runs **§6a SoT auto-apply**
   when appended follow-ups are present, updates the part ledger, and returns
   to §5.

**§6a. Squad Leader auto-apply approved SoT follow-ups (binding)**

After **part-planner** (§6 step 5) or **document-reviewer** (§7a step 8)
terminal, before returning to §5:

1. Read child `outputs` for `sotFollowUpPath`, `sotFollowUpStatus`,
   `sotFollowUpCount`, and folder binding (`localPath`).
2. When `sotFollowUpStatus: appended` and `sotFollowUpCount > 0`:
   - Parse **only** rows approved on the author or revision-author lane from
     the follow-up document.
   - Apply each approved change to paths under `<localPath>/source-of-truth/`
     per rule **20** — per-change structured choice on the child lane satisfies
     write authority (delegated approval).
   - Append matching entries to `<localPath>/source-of-truth/CHANGELOG.md`
     (date, paths, summary, approval locus: author lane `partId` or
     revision-author pass).
   - Optionally mark applied rows in the follow-up document; register updated
     SoT paths via **`mission_control_update_relevant_documents`** when material.
3. **Auto-advance** to §5 on success — **forbidden:** leader USER_CHECKPOINT to
   re-approve apply; deferring to a detached **`refresh source of truth`**
   dispatch for rows already approved on the child lane; prose-only "should I
   apply SoT?" handoff.
4. When `none` / `no-sot` / `skipped` or count 0 → §5 directly.
5. Apply failure (missing path, write error) → USER_CHECKPOINT (retry apply ·
   skip apply · abort) — exception path only.

**Part-planner open questions (binding — child lane):** Each open question,
concern, ambiguity, or incompleteness on the **part-planner** lane is asked via
**structured choice** (one `askQuestion.questions` entry per item; same modal may
batch). **Forbidden:** documenting open items only in the part plan and expecting
prose answers at plan review/approval. When items remain, co-present per-item
picks with Approve / Revise on the same approval turn — see
`skills/part-planner/SKILL.md` steps 4–5.

**Author draft→final review (binding — author lane):** Before **Confirm part
complete**, the author must run the **draft→final** structured-choice chain in
`skills/author/SKILL.md` step 5: after a draft write, offer **Approve draft →
write final copy** (or revise / explicit skip-to-final); offer part-complete
confirm only after finals exist or the developer explicitly skips. **Forbidden:**
jumping from first draft write to part-complete confirmation while content is
still draft-quality.

**Author Relevant Links pre-edit (binding — author lane):** After reading the
target document and **before** the first Write/StrReplace on the working file,
call **`mission_control_update_relevant_documents`** with the absolute document
path (`kind: other`; optional **`label`**: `partId`) — same turn preferred.
Re-register after subsequent material edits per `skills/author/SKILL.md` step 5.
**Forbidden:** material edit before first registration when the path is not yet
registered this session.

**Author SoT follow-up (binding — author lane):** After the user confirms the part
is complete, the author reviews the part conversation for SoT content that was
altered in practice, then runs one structured-choice question per identified
change and appends approved items to the **SoT changes follow-up document**
(additive to direct user SoT requests collected on the same document). See
`skills/author/SKILL.md`. **Zero-candidate path:** write conversation-review
evidence under ops docs (including count = 0) and open a USER_CHECKPOINT before
`none` / `no-sot` terminal result — **forbidden:** silent agent-only short-circuit.
**`none` semantics:** reviewed with zero approved proposals — not skipped review.
**Forbidden:** writing under **`source-of-truth/`** from this mission.

**Follow-up vs change log:** Author and revision-author lanes append approved
proposals only to the ops **SoT changes follow-up** document; the **Squad
Leader** applies them under **`source-of-truth/`** per **§6a** (including
**`CHANGELOG.md`** audit entries). **Forbidden:** child lanes appending to or
rewriting **`source-of-truth/CHANGELOG.md`**; treating that change log as default
SoT while authoring.

USER_CHECKPOINT — retry part-planner · skip/defer this part · abort after child failure.

### 7. Gap analysis with nested gap-closer (repeatable between parts)

- **Type:** Agent engagement and handover (nested: leader → gap-analyzer → gap-closer)
- **execution:** `spawned` (nested on gap-analyzer lane)
- **Intent:** Identify contradictions or misinterpretations between newly authored
  parts and previously authored parts; when gaps exist, close them on the
  gap-analyzer lane without Squad Leader re-spawn; then offer another analysis
  pass from the leader.
- **Inputs:** Paths/excerpts of authored parts; master plan; user focus hints;
  folder binding (`localPath`, `relativeFilePath`); `operationsDocsDirectory`.
- **Expected output:** Gap report; `gapsFound: true | false`; when closer runs,
  `gapsClosed` and `remainingGaps`; gap-analyzer `continuationStatus: terminal`.
- **Next-step resolution:** Analyzer terminal → post-gap gate (below). Post-gap
  gate → §7 again (repeat analysis) or §5.

**Target skill (Squad Leader spawn):** `skills/gap-analyzer/SKILL.md`

**Procedure (binding)**

1. **Squad Leader** spawns **`skills/gap-analyzer/SKILL.md`** with authored-part
   refs and folder binding. Open **#external-wait** before ending the turn.
2. **On the gap-analyzer lane:** write the gap report; set `gapsFound`.
3. **If `gapsFound: false`:** emit analyzer terminal result → Squad Leader
   post-gap gate.
4. **If `gapsFound: true`:** USER_CHECKPOINT on the gap-analyzer lane — spawn
   gap-closer with full report · spawn subset of proposed closer actions · skip
   closer (report only). **Forbidden:** Squad Leader spawning **gap-closer** on
   the happy path.
5. **On gap-analyzer lane after closer pick:** when the user chooses closer spawn,
   emit **`mission_control_spawn_agent`** for **`skills/gap-closer/SKILL.md`**
   with `gapReportPath`, `localPath`, `relativeFilePath`, `operationsDocsDirectory`,
   and optional `closerActions`. Keep **`continuationStatus: active`** until
   gap-closer terminal (mirror part-planner → author).
6. **On gap-closer terminal:** gap-analyzer merges closer outputs and emits **one**
   terminal **`mission_control_send_agent_result`** to Squad Leader.
7. **Squad Leader post-gap USER_CHECKPOINT** — run gap analysis again · start
   document comment review (§7a) · continue part delivery (§6) · return to §5
   standing options · pause. Include **`sync-documents`** per §5a.

USER_CHECKPOINT — run gap analysis again · start document comment review · continue next part · return to standing options · pause.

**Repeat runs (binding):** Multiple gap analysis passes often surface different
issues. Default to offering **run gap analysis again** after each analyzer/closer
cycle completes — do not treat one clean pass as permanent closure unless the user
explicitly stops requesting analysis.

### 7a. Document comment review (optional — after gap analysis or on demand)

- **Type:** Agent engagement and handover (nested: leader → document-reviewer →
  revision-author)
- **execution:** `spawned` (nested on document-reviewer lane)
- **Intent:** After authoring and gap analysis (or when the user requests from §5),
  offer to handle **review comments** embedded in the remote document. Sync from
  remote, inventory comments, produce an approved **review plan**, implement
  revisions, collect SoT follow-ups, then return to gap analysis or standing
  options.
- **Inputs:** Folder binding (`localPath`, `relativeFilePath`, rclone fields);
  `operationsDocsDirectory`; authored-part refs; optional `gapReportPath` from
  prior §7 pass; optional `sotFollowUpPath` when continuing an existing follow-up
  doc.
- **Expected output:** `reviewPlanPath`; `commentsFound: true | false`; when
  revisions run: updated document + SoT follow-up rows; `reviewComplete: true`;
  reviewer `continuationStatus: terminal`.
- **Next-step resolution:** Reviewer terminal → post-review gate (below).
  Post-review → §7 (gap analysis again) · §6 (next part) · §5.

**Leader opt-in gate (binding)**

Before spawning document-reviewer, Squad Leader opens structured choice:

> Handle review comments in the synced document now?

Options: **Start document comment review** · **Skip — return to standing options**
· **`sync-documents`** (§5a) · universal trailer.

**Forbidden:** auto-starting review without user opt-in after gap analysis.

**Target skill (Squad Leader spawn):** `skills/document-reviewer/SKILL.md`

**Procedure (binding)**

1. **Squad Leader** spawns **`skills/document-reviewer/SKILL.md`** with folder
   binding, document path, ops docs root, and optional gap-report pointer. Open
   **#external-wait** before ending the turn.
2. **On document-reviewer lane — sync & inventory:** Run inbound sync (same bisync
   / file-synchronizer contract as §9). Read the working document and flag **all
   review comments** (inline comments, suggestions, tracked-changes metadata —
   format-specific extraction per skill). Write **`reviewPlanPath`** under
   `operationsDocsDirectory` with one row per comment: id, location, comment
   text, proposed resolution, ambiguity flag.
3. **If `commentsFound: false`:** emit reviewer terminal (`commentsFound: false`)
   → Squad Leader post-review gate.
4. **If `commentsFound: true`:** For each row marked **ambiguous**, open
   structured choice on the document-reviewer lane (one question per item or
   batched modal — mirror part-planner open-questions binding).
5. **USER_CHECKPOINT (document-reviewer)** — approve review plan · revise plan ·
   skip implementation (report only).
6. **On approve:** document-reviewer spawns **`skills/revision-author/SKILL.md`**
   with `reviewPlanPath`, folder binding, `operationsDocsDirectory`, optional
   `sotFollowUpPath`. Keep **`continuationStatus: active`** until
   revision-author terminal (mirror part-planner → author).
7. **On revision-author lane:** Implement each approved review-plan row in the
   target document; run draft→final gates when material edits are large (reuse
   author step-5 pattern); after revisions, review conversation for SoT
   alterations and collect per-change approvals into the **SoT changes follow-up
   document** (same contract as `skills/author/SKILL.md` — **forbidden** writes
   under `source-of-truth/`).

**Revision-author Relevant Links pre-edit (binding — revision-author lane):**
After reading the target document and **before** the first Write/StrReplace on
the working file, call **`mission_control_update_relevant_documents`** with the
absolute document path (`kind: other`) — same turn preferred. Re-register after
subsequent material edits per `skills/revision-author/SKILL.md` step 5.
**Forbidden:** material edit before first registration when the path is not yet
registered this session.

**Revision-author SoT follow-up (binding — revision-author lane):** After the
user confirms revisions complete, the revision-author reviews the revision
conversation for SoT content that was altered in practice, then runs one
structured-choice question per identified change and appends approved items to
the **SoT changes follow-up document** (additive to direct user SoT requests).
See `skills/revision-author/SKILL.md`. **Zero-candidate path:** write
conversation-review evidence under ops docs (including count = 0) and open a
USER_CHECKPOINT before `none` / `no-sot` terminal result — **forbidden:** silent
agent-only short-circuit. **`none` semantics:** reviewed with zero approved
proposals — not skipped review. **Forbidden:** writing under **`source-of-truth/`**
from this mission.

8. **On revision-author terminal:** document-reviewer merges outputs (including
   SoT follow-up fields from revision-author) and emits **one** terminal
   **`mission_control_send_agent_result`** to Squad Leader.
9. **Squad Leader:** run **§6a SoT auto-apply** when merged outputs include
   appended follow-ups; then open **post-review USER_CHECKPOINT** — run gap analysis again (§7) ·
   continue next part (§6) · return to §5 standing options · run another comment
   review pass · pause. Include **`sync-documents`** per §5a.

USER_CHECKPOINT — run gap analysis again · continue next part · return to standing options · run comment review again · pause.

**Repeat passes (binding):** User may run §7a again after remote edits; do not
treat one clean pass as permanent closure.

### 8. Generate Content (content-generator)

- **Type:** Agent engagement and handover
- **execution:** `spawned`
- **Intent:** On Squad Leader / master-plan **Generate Content**, spawn
  **content-generator** to add content with chosen style and placement.
- **Inputs:** Document path; master plan; existing content-characteristic state
  when present.
- **Expected output:** Content written or proposed; updated characteristic state
  when newly defined.
- **Next-step resolution:** Child terminal → §5.

**Target skill:** `skills/content-generator/SKILL.md`

**Content characteristics (binding):**

1. If style, placement, and related characteristics are **already defined** for
   this document/dispatch, **do not** re-ask — proceed with them and offer an
   explicit option to **change** characteristics.
2. If not defined, ask style and placement (and related) before generating.

**Style options (illustrative — skill may extend):** flat · nested · with links ·
outline-only · Q&A blocks · tables-first · narrative-prose.

**Placement options (illustrative — skill may extend):** beginning · end ·
after named section/part.

USER_CHECKPOINT — after content-generator: keep characteristics · change characteristics · return to standing options.

Open **#external-wait** while the child runs.

